<p>I honestly have no idea what I was going for. I gave it a &quot;does this at least read as coherent in terms of content and SCP formatting&quot; check-through, and then I was like &quot;K, not even gonna analyze the rest of what I just wrote.&quot;</p>
<p>Usually I like writing things that are huge deals with great threats present, like <a href="/scp-2758">SCP-2758</a>, because I'm a drama llama. I guess this is one of the times I was seeing what would happen if I wrote a skip that was, like, chill. And not a huge threat and shit. I don't even know.</p>
<p>edit:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>so frustrating, in-universe, because there's no real way to figure out what's going on here, or reason with either of these two</p>
</blockquote>
<p>okay so TL333's gave me the words I was looking for. Yeah. These two are tied, the Foundation have no idea what the fuck is going on, but when they try to do <em>anything other than let them live on a plot of land and be high all the time,</em> everything goes to hell and people get hurt. It's a lesson in the Foundation needing to mind their own business and it's a lesson in anomalies not making sense, even in contexts other than physical and scientific.</p>
<p>I guess that's what I was going for.</p>

